              "audioEnd": 79.5
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Baba Yaga lived in a house that stood on chicken legs and moved around the forest.",
              "audioStart": 80.362,
              "audioEnd": 84.688
            },
            {
              "text": "When the old woman returned, she was angry to see a human child standing near her door.",
              "audioStart": 85.55,
              "audioEnd": 89.963
            },
            {
              "text": "Baba Yaga said that Vasilisa must work for her or else she would be eaten.",
              "audioStart": 90.825,
              "audioEnd": 94.612
            },
            {
              "text": "The bad woman gave her massive piles of grain to clean.",
              "audioStart": 95.475,
              "audioEnd": 98.45
            },
            {
              "text": "She also gave her terrible rooms to sweep before morning.",
              "audioStart": 99.312,
              "audioEnd": 102.25
            },
            {
              "text": "Baba Yaga thought that the girl could never finish all those difficult jobs in one night.",
              "audioStart": 103.112,
              "audioEnd": 107.412
            },
            {
              "text": "The bad woman laughed loudly and went to sleep.",
              "audioStart": 108.275,
              "audioEnd": 110.675
            },
            {
              "text": "Vasilisa sat alone in the dark room.",
              "audioStart": 111.537,
              "audioEnd": 113.713
            },
            {
              "text": "She looked at the huge piles of work and felt very sad.",
              "audioStart": 114.575,
              "audioEnd": 117.6
            },
            {
              "text": "The night was cold, and the wind blew hard against the walls.",
              "audioStart": 118.463,
              "audioEnd": 121.662
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Vasilisa began to cry because the work was too hard for one person to finish.",
              "audioStart": 122.525,
              "audioEnd": 126.987
            },
            {
              "text": "Then her special little toy spoke to her.",
              "audioStart": 127.85,
              "audioEnd": 129.875
            },
            {
              "text": "It told her to sleep while it did everything.",
              "audioStart": 130.738,
              "audioEnd": 132.775
            },
            {
              "text": "When the morning sun came up, all the work was completely finished.",
              "audioStart": 133.637,
              "audioEnd": 137.125
            },
            {
              "text": "The house was clean and quiet.",
              "audioStart": 137.988,
              "audioEnd": 139.7
            },
            {
              "text": "Baba Yaga was surprised, but she still had to let the girl try another difficult test.",
              "audioStart": 140.562,
              "audioEnd": 145.35
            },
            {
              "text": "The old woman watched the child carefully to see if she would fail the next task.",
              "audioStart": 146.213,
              "audioEnd": 150.275
            },
            {
              "text": "She did not believe that the girl could do it again.",
              "audioStart": 151.137,
              "audioEnd": 153.412
            },
            {
              "text": "Vasilisa felt much better after a good night of rest.",
              "audioStart": 154.275,
              "audioEnd": 157.3
            },
            {
              "text": "She knew her little toy was the best friend she could ever have.",
              "audioStart": 158.162,
              "audioEnd": 161.2
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "The woman gave her even more work to do while she went away on her flying pot.",
              "audioStart": 162.062,
              "audioEnd": 165.925
            },
            {
              "text": "Again, the little toy helped Vasilisa complete every single task before the sun went down.",
              "audioStart": 166.787,
              "audioEnd": 172.25
            },
            {
              "text": "Baba Yaga became very angry because she could not find any reason to hurt the bright girl.",
              "audioStart": 173.113,
              "audioEnd": 177.787
            },
            {
              "text": "The woman finally gave her a head bone with burning eyes to use as a light.",
              "audioStart": 178.65,
              "audioEnd": 182.45
            },
            {
              "text": "She told her to leave the dark house.",
              "audioStart": 183.312,
              "audioEnd": 185.075
            },
            {
              "text": "Baba Yaga wanted the light to test the girl.",
              "audioStart": 185.938,
              "audioEnd": 188.425
            },
            {
              "text": "She wanted to see what would happen when she returned home.",
              "audioStart": 189.287,
              "audioEnd": 191.838
            },
            {
              "text": "Vasilisa took the strange object and prepared to walk back.",
              "audioStart": 192.7,
              "audioEnd": 195.95
            },
            {
              "text": "The forest was still full of shadows, but she was ready.",
              "audioStart": 196.812,
              "audioEnd": 199.838
            },
            {
              "text": "Her power grew with every step she took.",
              "audioStart": 200.7,
              "audioEnd": 202.812
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "sentences": [
            {
              "text": "Vasilisa took the strange head bone and hurried back through the dark forest with the help of her toy.",
              "audioStart": 203.675,
              "audioEnd": 208.6
            },
            {
              "text": "When she arrived home, the bright eyes of the head bone looked right at the bad family members.",
              "audioStart": 209.463,
              "audioEnd": 214.15
            },
            {
              "text": "The bright fire from the head bone burned the bad family until they disappeared completely from the house.",
              "audioStart": 215.012,
              "audioEnd": 220.2
            },
            {
              "text": "After that, Vasilisa lived a happy life.",
              "audioStart": 221.062,
              "audioEnd": 223.75
            },
            {
              "text": "She never had to worry about bad people again.",
              "audioStart": 224.613,
              "audioEnd": 226.988
            },
            {
              "text": "She stayed in the small house and shared her days with friends who loved her very much.",
              "audioStart": 227.85,
              "audioEnd": 232.088
